THE FATE OF LIBERTY IN A TOTALITARIAN AGE
Visitors to Arendt’s gallery of the annals of “Western civilization” will find her walls similar to the ones the Cold War liberals curated. They were almost completely barren when it comes to the Enlightenment and nineteenthcentury liberalism. Yet she was as concerned as they were that the modern
